            <ArticleTitle>Understanding the pelvic pain mechanism is key to find an adequate therapeutic approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5301/uro.5000183</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is a natural mechanism to actual or potential tissue damage and involves both a sensory and an emotional experience. In chronic pelvic pain, localisation of pain can be widespread and can cause considerable distress. A multidisciplinary approach is needed in order to fully understand the pelvic pain mechanism and to identify an adequate therapeutic approach.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
